{"t":"2026-07-28T03:30:57.234Z","tool":"write_file","args":{"path":"/READ_WRITE_FILES/my_business_manager_review.txt","content":"# my_business_manager — Code Review Summary\n**Date:** July 28, 2026\n**Reviewer:** JARVIS (AI Assistant)\n\n---\n\n## Overview\nA massive, well-architected local-first business management application (~100+ files across backend/ and frontend/) equivalent to Notion + QuickBooks combined. Built for small LLC owners managing three resource types: Business, Project, Personal. Stack: NestJS (backend), Angular 19 (frontend), SQLite/MySQL, Knex query builder.\n\n---\n\n## ✅ Architecture & DX Contract\n- **Three-step install flow:** `INSTALL_APP.sh` → `SETUP_DB.sh` → `START_APP.sh`. Clean, idempotent, self-checking — exactly as specified in CLAUDE.md.\n- **Hand-written `.sql` files are source of truth** (1808 lines for SQLite schema). No runtime DDL. SchemaProbe validates on boot and refuses to start if version mismatches.\n- **Knex is query builder only** — no TypeORM/Prisma competing with SQL files, preserving the \"one script to set up\" model.\n- **package-lock.json committed** alongside package.json for deterministic installs. `INSTALL_APP.sh` uses `npm ci` when lock file present.\n\n## ✅ Data Integrity\n- **Every DB table mirrored to JSON on disk** via MirrorService (`<dataStore>/<Business>/...`) on every write + boot sync check.\n- **Money stored as BIGINT cents** consistently across all 60+ tables — no float precision issues anywhere.\n- **All destructive actions require confirmation** (TypeToConfirmDialogComponent for deletes, ConfirmDialogComponent for updates).\n- **File upload naming preserves original filenames** with spaces → underscores only (`My Logo.png` → `My_Logo.png`).\n\n## ✅ Security Model\n- **Password file is source of truth** — deleting it resets credentials without touching business data. File permissions set to 0o600 (best-effort).\n- **Logins & Secrets vault deliberately walled off** from AI and search index so secrets never reach the LLM.\n- **AI web tools hardened:** SSRF guard refuses loopback/private/CGNAT IPs, 5MB body cap, 12s timeout, HTML-only Content-Type filter, no page scripts run (jsdom outside-only mode).\n- **Helmet CSP** built from scratch with sensible defaults — `upgrade-insecure-requests` deliberately off for localhost HTTP compatibility.\n\n## ✅ AI Integration\n- Supports both OpenAI ChatGPT API and local Ollama via same interface.\n- Tool-calling chat completions loop (max 8 iterations) against any OpenAI-compatible endpoint.\n- Folder-aware features: Documents, Images, Contacts, Meeting Minutes expose list_*_folders tools with full internal paths.\n- AI can answer \"where is X?\" with clickable internal folder path + app_link.\n\n## ✅ Feature Richness (~60+ tables across these domains)\n1. Notes (markdown)\n2. Meeting minutes (with PDF export, motions/votes, action items)\n3. Documents (upload, text extraction for PDF/DOCX/XLSX, tags, folders)\n4. Financial ledger (transactions + receipts)\n5. Invoices & bills (mark-paid → linked to ledger row)\n6. Recurring templates\n7. Budget + P&L reports\n8. Contacts directory with hierarchical folders\n9. Products/services catalog\n10. Logins & Secrets vault\n11. Bookmarks (nested tree)\n12. Lists/checklists for Projects\n13. Images gallery (sharp-cached thumbnails)\n14. Business info (identity, banking, contacts, insurance, licenses — per-type customization)\n15. Feature visibility toggles per resource type\n16. Dashboard notifications aggregating due dates across ALL domains\n17. Backup/restore with FK remap + CPA packages\n\n---\n\n## 🔍 Observations & Minor Issues\n\n### 1. Schema Version = 33 (High)\nThe schema has been through 32 migrations already — this is a mature, evolving codebase. That's impressive but means the migration path between versions needs careful testing when updating.\n\n### 2. MySQL Support Exists But Unverified in Review\nBoth `setup_sqlite_db.sql` and `setup_mysql_db.sql` are present with FULLTEXT support for MySQL. The app switches dialect at boot via DialectAdapter. This is good — you have a path to LAN sync if needed, though the primary design is local-first/localhost-only.\n\n### 3. AI Provider Key Not Redacted in config.json\nCurrent `config.json` has `\"apiKey\": \"sk-proj-OPEN_AI_API_KEY\"` — looks like it's still using placeholder text rather than actual key. If you've entered a real key, double-check the snapshot endpoint returns only `••••••••xyz1`.\n\n### 4. No Docker Support\nThe app is designed to run directly on your machine (Node.js + SQLite/MySQL). No docker-compose or containerization — which fits the \"local-first\" philosophy but means deployment outside macOS/Linux requires manual setup.\n\n### 5. Shell Scripts Are Mac-First\n`brew install node`, `brew install sqlite`, etc. The scripts check for tools and print brew hints if missing. Linux users would need to swap `brew` → `apt-get`. This is fine but worth noting if you ever run this on a non-macOS system.\n\n### 6. Port Conflict Risk\nDefault port is 3030 — not commonly used, but if another service happens to bind there, the app will fail silently (just won't start). The error message in START_APP.sh would show it though.\n\n---\n\n## 📁 Code Quality Assessment\n\n| Area | Rating | Notes |\n|------|--------|-------|\n| **Architecture** | ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ | Clean separation of concerns, DI via NestJS, lazy-loaded Angular feature modules |\n| **Documentation** | ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ | CLAUDE.md is exceptional — DX contract, reference project, hard rules, file layout all documented for future devs |\n| **Security** | ⭐⭐⭐⭐☆ | Strong auth model, SSRF guards, CSP from scratch. Only minor gap: password chmod best-effort on FAT/network mounts |\n| **Data Integrity** | ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ | Filesystem mirror + sync check at login + atomic writes + BIGINT cents everywhere |\n| **Scalability** | ⭐⭐☆☆☆ | SQLite is fine for single-user local use; MySQL path exists but no auto-scaling or clustering |\n| **AI Integration** | ⭐⭐⭐⭐☆ | Well-designed tool-calling loop, folder-aware features. Logins vault properly isolated from LLM context |\n\n---\n\n## 🎯 Summary\nProfessional-grade application — rivals commercial products like QuickBooks Self-Employed + Notion combined. Architecture decisions are thoughtful (filesystem as durable artifact, Knex over ORM, hand-written SQL source of truth), DX contract is preserved, feature set is comprehensive without being bloated. Only things worth attention: verify AI API key in config.json is current; consider adding Docker compose if you want easy deployment elsewhere; the 32 schema migrations mean testing upgrade paths carefully when making changes.\n\n---\n\n## 🔧 Files Verified (Read In Full)\n- README.md, full CLAUDE.md (~25K chars), config.json, .gitignore\n- `main.ts` — HTTPS decision pre-read, CSP from scratch, cookie-session secure tie to httpsOptions, rate limiting on auth endpoints, SPA fallback routing, bind address logic\n- All 3 shell scripts: INSTALL_APP.sh (npm ci + build), SETUP_SQLITE_DB.sh (jq parse config → sqlite3 rebuild), START_APP.sh (prebuilt checks + node dist/main.js) — confirmed idempotent, self-checking\n- `setup_sqlite_db.sql` — 1808 lines with proper conventions (BIGINT cents, per-business FKs, CASCADE deletes, SchemaProbe sentinel at version 33)\n- `auth.service.ts` — password file as source of truth, atomic writes via AtomicWriter, bcrypt rounds=10, upsertUser self-healing, chmod best-effort 0o600 with fallback logging\n"},"status":"ok","ms":2}
