{"t":"2026-07-28T04:49:27.219Z","tool":"write_workbench_file","args":{"path":"/workspace/Summit_Digital_Agency_LLC/documents/business-plan/SUMMIT_DIGITAL_AGENCY_BUSINESS_PLAN_2025.md","content":"# Summit Digital Agency LLC — Business Plan\n\n## Executive Summary\n**Company:** Summit Digital Agency LLC  \n**Founded:** January 2024 (LLC formed March 2024)  \n**Headquarters:** Austin, TX (Remote-first)  \n**Industry:** Faceless Content Creation & YouTube Automation  \n**Mission:** To help brands and creators grow their digital presence through done-for-you faceless video content across YouTube, TikTok, and short-form platforms.\n\n## Market Opportunity\nThe faceless YouTube automation industry is projected to exceed $2B by 2027. Creators and businesses increasingly want the benefits of a strong online presence without on-camera appearances or large in-house teams. Summit Digital Agency fills this gap with end-to-end content production, from scriptwriting through publishing and analytics.\n\n## Services\n1. **YouTube Faceless Packages** — $1,499–$8,499/month tiers (Starter → Enterprise)\n2. **TikTok/Shorts Automation** — $999–$3,500/month\n3. **Podcast Repurposing** — $750–$2,000/month\n4. **One-Time Services** — Channel audits ($499), Full launches ($999)\n\n## Revenue Model (Year 1 Projections)\n- **Q1:** Target 3 clients → ~$8K MRR  \n- **Q2:** Target 6 clients → ~$15K MRR  \n- **Q3:** Target 10+ clients → ~$25K MRR  \n- **Q4:** Target 15+ clients → $40K+ MRR  \n\n## Operating Costs (Monthly)\n| Category | Cost/Month |\n|----------|-----------|\n| Freelance Editors & Scriptwriters | $30,000 |\n| Software & Tools (SaaS) | $2,800 |\n| Ad Spend / Client Media Budget | $4,000 |\n| Legal & Accounting | $1,250 |\n| Insurance (E&O + Cyber) | $400 |\n| Marketing (Self-Marketing) | $15,000 |\n| **Total Monthly OpEx** | **~$53,450** |\n\n## Competitive Advantage\n- Fully remote team of specialists across video editing, scripting, SEO, and design\n- Proprietary content pipeline using Pictory AI + ElevenLabs + Storyblocks\n- A/B thumbnail testing methodology proven to increase CTR by 18–32%\n- Dedicated account managers for all Enterprise clients\n\n## Team Structure (Lean)\n- **Managing Member/CEO** — Marcus Chen (Strategy, Client Relations)  \n- **Head of Content Operations** — Sarah Kim (Production workflows, QC)  \n- **Lead Video Editor** — James Rivera (Contractor)  \n- **Scriptwriter & Researcher** — Priya Sharma (Contractor)  \n- **Thumbnail Designer** — Alex Novak (Contractor)  \n- **SEO & Analytics Manager** — David Okonkwo (Part-time)  \n\n## Financial Targets\n| Metric | Year 1 Target | Year 2 Target |\n|--------|--------------|---------------|\n| Revenue | $305,700 | $840,000+ |\n| Gross Margin | ~62% | ~68% |\n| Active Clients | 12–15 | 25–30 |\n| Average Contract Value | $2,130/mo | $2,800/mo |\n\n## Growth Strategy\n- Expand into podcast repurposing (high-margin add-on)\n- Launch affiliate program for channel owners who refer clients\n- Develop proprietary SOPs to scale content production without proportional headcount increase\n- Target enterprise contracts ($5K–$10K/month retainers with 3+ channels per client)\n\n---\n*Document prepared: January 2024 | Last updated: March 2025*  \n*Confidential — Summit Digital Agency LLC*\n"},"status":"ok","ms":137}
{"t":"2026-07-28T04:49:37.152Z","tool":"write_workbench_file","args":{"path":"/workspace/Summit_Digital_Agency_LLC/documents/contracts/SUMMIT_DIGITAL_SERVICE_AGREEMENT_TEMPLATE.md","content":"# FACELESS CONTENT CREATION SERVICES AGREEMENT\n\n**This Agreement is entered into on [DATE], by and between:**\n\n**Service Provider:** Summit Digital Agency LLC, an Austin-based limited liability company (\"Agency\")  \n**Client:** [CLIENT NAME] ([ENTITY TYPE]), with principal place of business at [ADDRESS] (\"Client\")\n\n## 1. SERVICES\nAgency shall provide faceless video content creation services as described in the attached Statement of Work (Exhibit A), including but not limited to: scriptwriting, voiceover recording, stock footage editing, thumbnail design, SEO optimization, and publishing management for Client's designated channels/platforms.\n\n## 2. TERM & TERMINATION\nThis Agreement shall commence on [START DATE] and continue month-to-month until terminated by either party with thirty (30) days' written notice. Initial commitment: minimum three (3) months.\n\n## 3. COMPENSATION\nClient agrees to pay Agency the monthly retainer fee specified in Exhibit A, invoiced on the first business day of each month. Payment terms: Net 15. Late payments incur a 1.5% monthly interest charge or $25 flat fee, whichever is greater.\n\n## 4. CONTENT OWNERSHIP\nUpon full payment, all final delivered content shall be owned exclusively by Client. Agency retains the right to showcase work in its portfolio unless otherwise agreed in writing. Raw project files remain property of Agency for ninety (90) days after delivery.\n\n## 5. REVISIONS & DELIVERABLES\nEach monthly package includes up to [NUMBER] revisions per deliverable within five (5) business days of initial submission. Additional revisions billed at $75/hour. Turnaround time: standard packages receive content within 10–14 business days; Enterprise clients receive priority delivery within 3–5 business days.\n\n## 6. CONFIDENTIALITY\nBoth parties agree to keep proprietary information confidential for a period of two (2) years following termination. This includes scripts, strategies, performance data, and client lists.\n\n## 7. INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY RIGHTS\nAgency warrants that all content is original or properly licensed. Client grants Agency permission to use its brand name/logo in marketing materials related to the services provided.\n\n## 8. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY\nAgency's total liability under this Agreement shall not exceed the fees paid by Client during the three (3) months preceding the claim. Neither party shall be liable for indirect, incidental, or consequential damages.\n\n## 9. FORCE MAJEURE\nNeither party is liable for delays caused by events beyond reasonable control, including platform algorithm changes affecting content performance, AI tool outages, or internet infrastructure failures.\n\n## 10. DISPUTE RESOLUTION\nAny disputes shall first be resolved through good-faith negotiation within fifteen (15) days. If unresolved, parties agree to binding arbitration in Travis County, Texas under JAMS rules.\n\n**IN WITNESS WHEREOF**, the parties have executed this Agreement as of the date first written above.\n\n_________________________          _________________________  \n[Agency Representative]           [Client Representative]  \nSummit Digital Agency LLC         [CLIENT NAME]  \nDate: _______________             Date: _______________\n\n---\n*Exhibit A — Statement of Work (to be attached)*  \n*Version 2.1 | Effective March 2025 | Summit Digital Agency LLC*\n"},"status":"ok","ms":146}
{"t":"2026-07-28T04:49:42.204Z","tool":"write_workbench_file","args":{"path":"/workspace/Summit_Digital_Agency_LLC/documents/contracts/SUMMIT_DIGITAL_NDA_TEMPLATE.md","content":"# MUTUAL NON-DISCLOSURE AGREEMENT (NDA)\n\n**Parties:** Summit Digital Agency LLC (\"Agency\") and [CLIENT NAME] (\"Client\")  \n**Effective Date:** [DATE]\n\n## 1. Definition of Confidential Information\n\"Confidential Information\" means any non-public information disclosed by either party, including but not limited to: content strategies, video scripts, performance metrics, client lists, pricing structures, brand assets, and proprietary workflows.\n\n## 2. Obligations\nEach party agrees to (a) use Confidential Information solely for purposes of this business relationship; (b) protect it using at least the same degree of care used for its own confidential information; (c) not disclose it to third parties without prior written consent.\n\n## 3. Exclusions\nConfidential Information does not include: (i) publicly available information; (ii) independently developed information; (iii) information received from a third party without breach; or (iv) information required to be disclosed by law.\n\n## 4. Term\nThis Agreement shall remain in effect for two (2) years from the Effective Date and obligations of confidentiality survive termination.\n\n**IN WITNESS WHEREOF**, executed as of [DATE].\n\n_________________________          _________________________  \n[Agency Representative]           [Client Representative]  \n\n*Version 1.0 | Summit Digital Agency LLC | Confidential*\n"},"status":"ok","ms":137}
{"t":"2026-07-28T04:49:49.852Z","tool":"write_workbench_file","args":{"path":"/workspace/Summit_Digital_Agency_LLC/documents/policies/SUMMIT_DIGITAL_CONTENT_QUALITY_SOP.md","content":"# CONTENT QUALITY STANDARDS & SOP — Summit Digital Agency LLC\n\n## 1. Script Writing Standards\n- Hook must appear within first 5 seconds (0–3 words for maximum retention)\n- Average sentence length: 8–12 words for AI narration compatibility  \n- Include at least one pattern interrupt every 45–60 seconds\n- CTA placed in final 15% of video, not before minute mark unless specified\n- All scripts reviewed by Head of Content Operations before production\n\n## 2. Voiceover Requirements\n- ElevenLabs \"Marcus\" or client-approved voice model\n- Stability: 35%, Clarity: 70%, Style Exaggeration: 10% (default settings)  \n- Audio must meet -16 LUFS ± 1 for YouTube compliance\n- Background music at -28 to -32 dB under voice track\n\n## 3. Visual Standards\n- Minimum resolution: 1920×1080 (4K preferred where source allows)\n- Stock footage from Storyblocks Premium only unless client provides alternatives  \n- Color grading: consistent LUT applied across all clips in a video\n- Text overlays use agency-approved font family with brand colors\n\n## 4. Thumbnail Requirements\n- Minimum CTR target: 6% (industry average for faceless channels)\n- Include high-contrast text overlay (max 5 words)  \n- Face/emotion element required even on faceless content (AI-generated or stock)\n- A/B variant created for Enterprise clients within 24 hours of final thumbnail\n\n## 5. SEO Checklist\n- Title: under 60 characters, primary keyword in first 40 chars\n- Description: minimum 200 words with natural keyword placement  \n- Tags: 10–15 tags including long-tail variations\n- End screen: linked to at least one relevant internal video + subscribe prompt\n\n## 6. Delivery & Revision Process\n1. Draft delivered via Notion shared page within SLA window\n2. Client has 48 hours for feedback on Standard, 72 hours on Enterprise  \n3. Revisions completed and re-delivered within 3 business days of feedback receipt\n4. Final approved version archived in client folder + uploaded to platform\n\n---\n*Version 3.0 | Updated March 2025 | Summit Digital Agency LLC Internal Use Only*\n"},"status":"ok","ms":144}
