{"t":"2026-07-28T17:12:34.234Z","tool":"plan_create","args":{"objective":"Create a web-based Doom-style first-person shooter game playable in the browser using a .js framework with retro 90s graphics, served on an exposed port (9101-9150), and save the full source code to the shared folder.","steps":["Select and set up a suitable JavaScript 3D engine/framework for retro FPS (e.g., Three.js, Babylon.js).","Design and implement a simple retro-style map, player movement, and shooting mechanics.","Add basic AI enemies with simple behaviors (patrol, chase, damage player).","Integrate retro-style textures, sounds, and UI elements reminiscent of 90s FPS games.","Test the game locally to ensure all core mechanics (movement, shooting, enemies, win/lose conditions) work.","Set up a Node.js static server to serve the game on an available port between 9101-9150 and verify browser access.","Save the complete source code to /READ_WRITE_FILES for user access.","Provide the user with the game access link and instructions in chat."]},"status":"ok","ms":4}
